From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add karpenter admission check to provision nodeclaims for admitted workloads

Admitted workloads scheduled onto dynamic cloud capacity experience prolonged scheduling delays and pod startup timeouts while waiting for generic node autoscalers to detect unschedulable pods. Standard cloud autoscalers reactively provision nodes only after pods fail scheduling and emit events. When Kueue admits high-priority distributed workloads, it knows the exact resource flavors, node pools, and capacity requirements before ungating pods, but lacks a mechanism to trigger just-in-time node provisioning directly.

Implement a Karpenter AdmissionCheck controller in Kueue that reconciles admitted Workloads against Karpenter NodePool and NodeClaim custom resources. Provision dedicated NodeClaim objects matching the workload's admitted flavor and pod count, holding workload admission checks in a pending state until NodeClaims become Launched (or Registered when configured), and inject anti-theft taints, tolerations, and node selectors to isolate provisioned capacity.
---
